# AI Working State
Last updated: 2026-08-08 (v4.3.2)

Small on purpose: where the work stopped, where the detail lives, and the
cross-cutting decisions that must not be re-litigated. Everything that can be
read off the code, CLAUDE.md, CHANGELOG.md or git history is deliberately NOT
here.

Read this first. Then read `state/<track>.md` for the track you are touching —
and only that one.

## Latest
**v4.3.2** (2026-08-08, `c0ef33f`, CONFIRMED fixed on device): framed pages are
denied a scroll region
(`overflow:hidden` + 2px slack) because Chromium does not chain a scroll out of a
frame — one scrollable pixel in the framed document consumed the whole gesture
and painted the overscroll glow, which is what the Heating tab was doing before
every drag. Third attempt at this bug; the first two (v4.3.0 sizing, v4.3.1
render-skip + viewport-sized growth) were inferred from symptoms. None of it
reproduces in headless Chromium at any DPR — the device is the only verdict, so
ASK WHAT THE FAILURE LOOKS LIKE before theorising. Detail: `state/ui-shell.md`.

Before that, **v4.3.0**: the shell stopped scrolling the framed page (`dbb0cda`,
confirmed on Android for Batteries) and the Batteries page grew a per-row
Ignore/Track button (`a734f9c`). Detail: `state/bundled-examples.md`.

